  pw=30 pr=50:    0 of  250 seeds expose it; p = 0.0000, 95% CP [0.0000, 0.0146]
      zero failures: the 95% upper bound is 0.0119, and the bug is there
  pw=70 pr=50:  250 of  250 seeds expose it; p = 1.0000, 95% CP [0.9854, 1.0000]
  even mix: seeds for a 99% chance of one exposure: 18
  clean streaks before an exposure: 236 streaks, longest 19, mean 3.23 (geometric mean (1-p)/p = 3.24)
  cycle of first exposure: min 40, median 135, max 199
  first exposures by window [0,50) [50,100) [100,150) [150,200): [3, 56, 84, 93]

